based on a true story is the oldest  trick in Hollywood's book and horror  fans have seen variations on that idea  countless times the blurry or the line  between fact and fiction the bigger the  potential scares right but sometimes the  stories behind the scenes are even more  terrifying here's some horror movies  based on even scarier true stories  Dracula  Bram Stoker's classic story has been  revisited countless times in cinema  making it some of the most beloved  source material of all time but until  Francis Ford Coppola 's 1992 film Bram  Stoker's Dracula the connection between  Dracula and historical figure vlad Drac  had never been depicted on screen if you  think a pale immortal vampire poised to  suck your blood is scary consider Vlad  the Impaler  a Transylvanian noble is thought to have  tortured and executed as many as a  hundred thousand peasants and civilians  during his reign deeming the poor is  useless to society he had them slowly  impaled from bottom to top and then  hoisted publicly for display so which is  scarier the Fang or the pole The  Exorcist the oscar-winning 1973 film The  Exorcist was based on the 1949 position  of a Maryland boy named Roland doe who  reportedly underwent an exhausting  battery of exorcism performed by Jesuit  priests while skeptics maintain the  dough was insane the phenomenon of  demonic possession has been traced at  biblical times and is taken very  seriously by religious experts while  neither spinning heads nor projectile  vomit has been wildly reported  levitations shaking beds and speaking in  tongues have not scared yet well  consider that the demand for exorcisms  has rapidly increased in recent years in  2015 the Catholic Church reported having  as many as a hundred requests at any  given time The Amityville Horror the  house at 112 Ocean Avenue in Amityville  Long Island is an icon of the horror  genre having inspired the Amityville  horror film franchise but what  transpired at the actual address is more  horrific than anything to take it in a  franchise they are 24 year-old Ron de  feo brutally murdered his mother father  and four younger siblings with a shotgun  in 1974 the hotly contested account in  Jansen's book details the bizarre events  that followed the house reportedly stood  empty for 13 months until the Lutz  family moved in only to abruptly flee  after 28 days claiming they had been  terrorized by paranormal phenomena after  extensive paranormal investigations for  decades subsequent owners remodeled the  exterior and  no longer even listed as 112 Ocean  Avenue the house is still standing  though and for just a low low price of  eight hundred and fifty thousand dollars  it too can be yours the Serpent and the  rainbow zombies are all the rage as The  Walking Dead and privately every other  TV show and video games seem to prove in  Wes Craven's 1988 voodoo horror film the  serpent in the rainbow however we find a  very different kind of zombie it's  loosely adapted from a nonfiction book  of the same name by ethnobotany suede  Davis who outlined his expeditions to  Haiti investigating the bizarre case of  clairvius narcisse  a man who had reportedly returned from  the dead according to Narcisse he was  administered a puffer fish toxin after  offending a voodoo sorcerer as a result  he collapsed and was pronounced dead but  he was actually conscious during the  delivery of his death certificate and  witnessed his own burial from inside the  casket he was recovered from his grave  two days after his funeral and was  enslaved forced to work on a sugar  plantation Narcisse was finally released  and returned to his village 18 years  later where the dead man reunited with  his sister so happy ending kinda a  terrifying  Ed Gein some of the scariest and  best-known characters in horror have  been based on the serial killer at gain  Dean's grisly murder spree inspired  Leatherface of the Texas Chainsaw  Massacre Norman Bates of psycho and  Buffalo Bill of The Silence of the Lambs  just to name a few  in fact Dean's actual crimes were so  heinous that he might be the most  monstrous figure in American history  beguin family wasn't exactly a Norman  Rockwell portrait to begin with his  father and two brothers passed away  early in his life after the passing of  his sole companion his beloved mother  ian lived alone in their rural Wisconsin  farmhouse the mild-mannered handyman  didn't attract much attention to 12  years following her death but when a  neighboring a hardware store owner  disappeared in 1957 ian came under  suspicion and a search of his property  revealed the decapitated woman in a shed  splayed out like a free skinned deer  inside the house authorities found masks  wastebaskets and lampshades made from  human skin along with assorted human  remains in fact some of what was  discovered as far too grisly to mention  here but suffice it to say genes living  room would make leather face plush it  was later determined that he'd also been  making late-night visits to nearby  cemeteries exhuming women who looked  like his mother  this room was found boarded up and  completely untouched Ian's story even  sans chainsaw is truly the stuff of  nightmares thanks for watching subscribe  to our YouTube channel to watch  less scary videos like the one you just  saw and leave us a comment to let us  know which of these true stories is  scarier than fiction  [Music]
 

